From f3d508f479135fb5a27a8168f96c5ae8cb278fb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: csolomon <charliesolomon@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:25:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] offline-model-data: build without the vendor catalogue fetch

Re-authored 2026-09-02: gah-model-data.ts now writes src/providers/data/
in place instead of staging under a mkdtemp directory and swapping it in.
On a managed Windows machine the final rmSync of the staging directory
failed with EPERM ("Permission denied: ...\.model-generation-XXXX"),
which is what antivirus holding a handle on just-scanned files looks like.
The output is deterministic so there is nothing to roll back to; stale
provider files from an earlier hydration are unlinked individually, and
the result is validated the same way. No directory rename or recursive
delete remains in the step.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011it956DeV4unyWw5VyvkDD

Re-authored 2026-09-22 (sync to v0.87.1): upstream 0.86 added a Radius
provider that spreads Object.values() of its catalogue. Seeded empty, that
catalogue types its values as unspreadable (TS2698) and the ai package
fails to build. One cast in src/providers/radius.ts, same shape either way.
It belongs here because the empty seed is what this patch introduces.

Re-authored 2026-09-30 (sync to v0.99.1): upstream moved generated model
data to schema 6 (#9948), which keys every entry "<type>:<id>" and
requires a type on each. A seed copied from an older hydration failed
the validator with one error per model, and Bedrock's ids made it
unreadable: the colon in `amazon.nova-pro-v1:0` was taken as the
separator, so the report said type `amazon.nova-pro-v1`, id `0`, 281
times. gah-model-data.ts now refuses a seed key with no model type and
names the fix (`make refresh-model-data`). The build script keeps
upstream's move from tsgo to tsc; generate-image-models is gone upstream.

The same empty seed breaks four more providers the way it broke Radius:
cloudflare-workers-ai, opencode, openrouter and vercel-ai-gateway now
spread their chat and classifier (and, for openrouter, image) catalogues
into createProvider<Api>() with an explicit API type, and an empty
catalogue's values type as unknown. One `as never[]` on each models
array; an empty catalogue holds no models, so the cast asserts nothing
false. A single fix in model-catalog.ts was tried and rejected: the
simple providers infer their API type from the chat catalogue, and no
empty-catalogue type satisfies both kinds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WHU6GR6xxBMmQZUcB1KhgK
